1
00:00:03,214 --> 00:00:05,866
Day ten of the twelve days of Fabric Apps:

2
00:00:05,866 --> 00:00:08,454
a snow globe that decides who stays home.

3
00:00:08,904 --> 00:00:12,446
At five in the morning someone calls a snow day from

4
00:00:12,446 --> 00:00:16,124
a weather app and a hunch, and nobody writes down why.

5
00:00:17,705 --> 00:00:20,740
Every site is a building on its own hill, as high

6
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:24,085
as the site; snow falls over each one at its forecast.

7
00:00:24,535 --> 00:00:28,344
The windows are the call: warm is open, dark is closed,

8
00:00:28,344 --> 00:00:32,015
and the faint flicker means nobody has called it yet.

9
00:00:32,828 --> 00:00:36,462
Turn the dial to tomorrow and the storm arrives: thirty-four

10
00:00:36,462 --> 00:00:40,218
centimetres on the ridge, and the rural roads disappear first.

11
00:00:44,970 --> 00:00:48,276
The decision lens rings each hill with the call in

12
00:00:48,276 --> 00:00:51,120
force; four of ten sites are called so far.

13
00:00:53,205 --> 00:00:56,815
Today ranks what needs me before the nine o’clock lock.

14
00:00:57,265 --> 00:01:00,783
This one flies to Harbour Lane: closed at two percent,

15
00:01:00,783 --> 00:01:03,845
against the model, and the reason is on record.

16
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:08,840
A site lead sees their own sites, and the forecast they still owe.

17
00:01:19,466 --> 00:01:23,476
On The call, the model is a logistic regression fitted to

18
00:01:23,476 --> 00:01:27,486
our own past calls, and it shows what drives each number.

19
00:01:27,936 --> 00:01:31,838
Ridge Road Clinic is at ninety-two percent. If I open it

20
00:01:31,838 --> 00:01:36,576
anyway, that goes against the model by more than thirty-five points.

21
00:01:37,026 --> 00:01:40,085
So a two-word reason is refused; it needs thirty

22
00:01:40,085 --> 00:01:43,016
characters that say what the model cannot see.

23
00:01:43,822 --> 00:01:47,271
After nine the day is locked: a change becomes a

24
00:01:47,271 --> 00:01:51,222
revision, and the call it replaces stays in the record.

25
00:01:52,034 --> 00:01:55,115
Hindsight scores every past call against what the

26
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:59,264
day brought: ninety percent right, fifteen closures over-cautious.

27
00:01:59,714 --> 00:02:05,004
Next winter’s call starts from last winter’s record, not a hunch.
